WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.190
Thank you.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.190
Good evening, Senator.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:05.860
Good evening, Becker.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.470
If you don't mind waiting here for just a moment, I'll tell my brother you're here.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:40.410
Thank you, Senator.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.300
My brother will see you now.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.110
Thank you.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.180
Thanks for the lift from the station.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.100
Good evening.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.420
Good evening.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.620
My brother, the senator, has told you we're in mourning here.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.760
My nephew died recently.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:55.690
Yes, I know.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.960
So I presume your business must be very important down here.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:03.550
Thank you. I came here because I happened to read of his death.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.580
You read the funeral announcement. You must have noticed that the services were limited only to the family.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.200
Isn't a man's widow a member of the family?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.260
There is a widow, Miss Marshall.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.700
My maiden name was Sandra Marshall. My married name is Mrs. James Caldwell Demarest.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.240
I am your nephew's widow.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:29.970
I'd better postpone.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.200
I don't know my condolences until I learn a few more of the facts.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.330
This is my marriage license.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.460
Jim's papers include no copy of this.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.500
Perhaps he had a hidden safe deposit box.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:46.980
We'll check on it.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.930
If I hadn't happened to see that notice,

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.830
I would have known nothing of my husband's death.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.240
He would have been safely buried and out of the way

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.380
by the time I discovered it.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:55.380
Safely buried?

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.010
That's a strange expression, Miss Marshall.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.790
My name is Mrs. Demarest.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.620
I should prefer to be called that.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:02.990
Of course.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.220
But I'm afraid I must insist upon a little more proof

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.360
than this copy of a license,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.920
which I'm by no means sure is genuine.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.480
The reason for this secret marriage...

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.300
I'm not sure it was secret to you.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.220
Come now, Mrs. Demarest.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.910
If I'm to believe you, you must believe me.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:23.410
But he must have told you.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:24.860
Why do you say that?

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.340
Because he wanted his inheritance.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.040
He had to be married in order to get it.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:29.970
What would have been the use of the marriage...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.380
otherwise? I don't follow you. The will. What will? The will you encourage Jim's mother to draw up.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:39.980
Surely you remember one clause of it. I suppose you refer to the one which keeps Jim and his

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:45.440
sisters money in trust until they reach the age of 30. It always annoyed Jim. Do you wonder?

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.330
You made yourself guardian of his fortune. It must have been extremely difficult for a grown

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:55.620
man to have to ask his uncle for money when he had the right to millions. Difficult, not insupportable.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.970
Even that might be forgivable but certainly not the fact that if he married the control immediately passed

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.910
No doubt you intended to choose that wife yourself,

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.900
some nice placid girl who would do what you told her.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.510
Jim is smarter than you thought. He married me.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.970
And I am not a placid girl.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.980
No, I'm not.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:22.490
Might I ask where he found you?

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.000
We knew one another at college.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.350
I was working for my doctor's degree in geology.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.370
Do your parents know this marriage?

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.620
No, they're both dead.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:34.900
Were you in love with him?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.630
No, he came to me as a friend and I helped him.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:42.420
Helped him?

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.560
And exactly what did you get out of helping him?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.290
I needed money.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.190
He gave me $2,000 to complete my studies.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.830
I was to divorce him after six months.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:54.820
There were no other strings.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.620
We were married five months. Jim's death was quite convenient, wasn't it?

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.150
$2,000 has now become $2 million.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.720
What do you intend to do?

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:17.820
I shall claim the Wrights left me in his will.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.200
But he left no will.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.180
I don't know where the original is, but here's the copy.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:29.630
Signatures.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:35.270
I happen to know there is an original, completely attested.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.550
If you don't find it, I shall be forced to claim my entire rights.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.360
You know, if I were to bring this battle of wits down to direct insults,

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:47.280
I'd say you were one of the most cold-blooded, scheming women I've ever met in my life.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.770
You've already said that.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.880
For the moment, we'll let it rest there.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.560
For Jim's sake, as well as the rest of the family,

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.000
I'd prefer there were no unpleasantness tonight.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.300
You have to stay the night, but before you left in the morning.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.480
Would it be possible for me to see...

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.720
Your husband? No, casket is closed.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.260
You will, however, allow me to pay my last respects.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.990
Now, Mark, before you say a word, I can't go through with it.

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.510
I'm going back to Washington at once.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:08.680
Not deeper, if I may say so.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:09.460
No, I'm not.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:10.760
Keep your voice down, will you?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:11.850
The girl's in there.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:12.930
Well, who is she, anyway?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:13.730
Why is she here?

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.590
I'll tell you later.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.960
My housekeeper, Martha, will show you to your room.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:34.910
Thank you.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:52.830
This way, madame.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:08.880
Sorry, I hope I haven't kept you waiting.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.830
Holly, let me do introduce you to Sandra Demarest.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:31.210
Your sister-in-law.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.340
My sister-in-law?

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.090
Yes, Jim's widow.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:37.990
I'm very glad to know you, Julie.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:40.560
I'm stunned.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:44.150
Completely, absolutely stunned.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.180
You're not a bit Jim's type.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.460
Oh, I don't mean you're not awfully attractive because you are, but...

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.940
Why, it's stupendous, that's what it is.

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.900
Will Amy Daniels be mad?

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:55.140
Well, it serves her right.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.470
Santa, tell me all about it, please, please.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.650
We will, Julie, if you'll control yourself.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:01.500
It was a secret marriage.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.140
Oh, how exciting, Sandra.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.690
I'm going to start calling you, Sandra, right off.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.400
Anyway, I'm awfully glad you're here.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.180
You'll stay for a long time, won't you?

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.000
Mrs. Demarest is not prepared to stay.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:13.920
Why not?

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.210
I have a suitcase checked at the station.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.250
Well, in that case, Becky can bring your suitcase up in the morning.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:19.890
Thank you.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.010
Good. That's settled.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:29.350
How about this letter mark?

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.100
May I ask what rate you had to read it?

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.690
I didn't read it, my dear. I wanted the address and it wasn't on the envelope.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.520
Look, if you think you're going to bust up this romance, you're very much mistaken.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.680
I hardly think this is the proper time to discuss marriage proposals.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.360
Oh, who said anything about proposals?

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:47.680
What do you want me to do, stick here in this awful mausoleum for the rest of my life?

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.020
We'll discuss it later, Julie.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.140
No, we won't.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:51.790
Sit down.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.310
Not Judy.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:47.460
Yes. Yes, of course, Julie.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:51.440
I'd have come before, but Marta was hanging around.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.220
She's always spying on me.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:57.270
And that wasn't very nice of me to talk about Amy Daniels.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.520
But Jim was always mad about her until...

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.350
Well, I suppose after she let him down flat.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.020
Did she really turn him down?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.660
Oh, she turned him down all right.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.340
It was so strange.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:12.880
They were engaged.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.270
I know they both were crazy about each other.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.800
She'd been here playing tennis the day before it happened.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.180
And they were spooning about something fierce.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.700
And then, the very next day, it went poof.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:25.960
Don't you think that's strange?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.210
Yes, I do.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.000
Did Jim say anything about Mark to you?

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:35.280
A few things. Why?

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.960
I think Mark was the one who broke it off.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.160
He's always managed to stop Jim from doing anything he wanted.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:45.440
Why, Jim could have done so many good, fine things with his money.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.870
But I guess you know about the money.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.360
Yes, I know.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.310
But Mark didn't think so.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:56.110
He said Jim was a dreamer, an idealist.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.900
So now he's using the money for his laboratory, his plan.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.540
his ideas believe those are dangerous accusations that money's in trust that won't stop mark i know

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:13.420
him for what he is and he'll twist you around his finger like he does everybody else believe

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:29.900
me julie that won't happen you're imagining things aren't you that's what mark said

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.000
He says I'm always imagining things.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.820
You won't ever let on to him about what we've been saying,

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.680
no matter how he tries to pry it out of you.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.140
You know I won't.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:43.870
I knew you were regular.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.040
Why, this is attractive.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:50.720
It's very old.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:51.580
It came from Florence.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:53.400
It belonged to my mother.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.460
It's late. I suppose you want to go to bed.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:05.820
I am tired.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:11.210
Then I'm off. I don't want Marty to start snooping.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:16.860
Julie, what did Jim die of?

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.980
Pneumonia. Didn't Mark tell you?

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.400
No, he didn't.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.980
He'd been in Canada, came home late at night.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:39.410
I heard his voice in the library. I'm sure I did the next morning. Mark said he was ill and you never saw him again

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:48.040
They put him in the laboratory. I'm never allowed in there. Oh Sandra, please stay here

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:53.570
I'm so terribly lonely in this house. Nobody to talk to people looking at me all the time

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:57.620
Promise me you'll stay stay as long as I can

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:01.480
Good night, Sandra.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:02.460
Good night, Julie.

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.770
I think I'm going to like having a sister.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.010
Same here.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:30.100
Thank you.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:16.520
going to the library? I'm sorry, I must get back to Washington. One moment, Charles.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.980
You go in with the others, will you? I'll join you in a moment.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:38.660
I've done what's expected of me, Mark. I've put in an appearance at the funeral. Now, you can't ask for anything more.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.480
It's a question of Jim's will. You should be here.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.340
No, no, I don't want anything to do with it.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.540
I hope you won't regret this.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.520
I hope you won't, Mark.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:54.610
This whole thing has been a great shock to us. We weren't prepared for it.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.800
So it'll take a certain amount of time to...

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.880
Oh, Mark, I've been explaining to Mrs. Demarest...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.160
We're making every effort to locate Jim's deposit box.

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:03.480
How long will it take?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.100
Two weeks, I should say.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.180
Oh, then Sandra can stay. I'm so glad.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:08.950
Of course, Mrs. Gunrasse will stay.

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.180
I want her to be entirely satisfied about everything.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.420
By the way, I think you should keep this death certificate.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:16.650
May I look at it, please?

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:18.860
Certainly.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.660
Ike, you'll find it quite in order.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.220
Signed by the local doctor and undertaker.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.130
May I keep it?

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.920
Of course, you're Jim's widow.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:29.190
Can't we skip all these gruesome details?

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:29.970
It's going to be a...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.540
It's been a nice day. Can't we go for a ride, Sandra and I?

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.750
Mrs. Demarest may not care for riding.

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.310
I'd like it. It would be pleasant to get some sunshine.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:38.680
But I haven't any...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.420
Don't worry about a riding habit. I can find something for you. Come on.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:49.440
Mrs. Demarest, I have no objection to your going riding,

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.380
but I wish you wouldn't let Julie take you off the estate.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:55.050
Don't you think you're holding too tight a leash on her?

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:56.060
No.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.970
I saw her yesterday. Jumping fences, dashes...

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.200
You can't bottle up all that energy very long.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.240
Oh, I must still insist.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.510
But if she doesn't get around and meet people of her own age,

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.970
how will she learn discrimination?

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:12.330
Discrimination?

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:17.150
If Julie exercises as much discrimination as you did about men,

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.690
she might not find it resulted so profitable, would she?

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.790
I rather asked for that one, didn't I?

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.020
Beautiful here in the woods.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.440
Sandra, you're going to think me an awful heel.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.720
I brought you writing under false pretenses.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.440
Julie, we haven't left the estate.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.250
No, I'm meeting Ronnie.

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:57.180
Ronnie?

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:58.810
Yes, Ronnie Manning.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:19:59.980
The man who wrote the letter.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.470
that Mark opened. That's why I was so thrilled when the sun came out. I was afraid we wouldn't

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:10.550
be able to make it. Do you think you should? Why not? How do I know how much longer Mark

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:16.420
will let me leave the house, let alone ride? Why do you say such things? You'll find out.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.590
Come and meet him.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.500
No, you go ahead. I'll wait here.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:01.310
Where's Julie?

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.670
Why, she was right behind me.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.210
I'll ride back and see what's happened, Paul.

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.110
She's meeting Manning, isn't she?

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.500
I was hoping you'd be more sensible about Julie,

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.240
but I'm afraid you're incurably romantic.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.570
I'm no chaperone. Don't ask me to be one again.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.800
It's very important for Julie to be straightforward.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.100
Things like this don't help.

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:25.730
Do you think the atmosphere of this place is conducive to being straightforward?

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.220
Please accept my handling of Julie.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.720
I've asked you once.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.080
Now I'm asking you again.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:32.070
Lanza!

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:41.600
How long have you been here?

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.060
I wish you hadn't done this, Julie.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.000
Especially after promising me.

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:48.360
And I'm afraid Mr. Manning won't like what I have to tell him either.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.810
How dare you spy on me?

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:53.100
I won't stand it! I won't!

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:04.700
Now, Mrs. Demarest will please excuse us.

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:09.330
I'd like a word with you, Dan, please.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:11.010
Get down.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:25.050
He'll be along, Mr. Marcus with her.

00:22:25.480 --> 00:22:27.320
You ride so wild, I get scared.

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:29.970
Now, what's your riding in? You sit a horse with...

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:39.020
Tell me Roberts, do they use the rear wing of the house?

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.210
Oh, yes, ma'am. That's Mr. Colwell's laboratory.

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:43.520
Thank you.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.880
Sandra, you did, didn't you? Julie, what is it?

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.780
You heard it, didn't you? I didn't imagine it.

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:36.530
Julie, shh, quiet, you'll wake everybody.

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.970
I've heard it before, a week ago, that Mark says I have nightmares.

00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:43.090
That isn't true, I do hear it. Hear what?

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:47.690
Voices, people scuffling, a man crying out as if he were in agony.

00:23:47.970 --> 00:23:52.040
You heard that tonight? Yes, and it sounded like Jim's voice.

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:56.000
Jim's voice? Oh, no, Julie, it couldn't be.

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:41.300
the other wing of the house.

00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:42.400
Repertory?

00:24:43.110 --> 00:24:43.390
There.

00:24:43.730 --> 00:24:45.130
But it's locked, it's always locked.

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:48.090
That's where it must have come from.

00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:11.420
I don't know what's going on in this house, but I'm going to find out.

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:12.660
Santa, please stay with me tonight.

00:26:13.060 --> 00:26:14.360
No, you'll be all right.

00:26:14.460 --> 00:26:15.320
When I leave, lock the door.

00:26:15.540 --> 00:26:17.080
In the morning, tell Mark what you heard.

00:26:17.220 --> 00:26:18.000
Oh, no, I couldn't.

00:26:18.100 --> 00:26:19.880
If he finds I've left my room, they'll lock me in.

00:26:19.940 --> 00:26:20.740
They did once before.

00:26:20.940 --> 00:26:22.080
Don't tell him you left the room.

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.360
And remember, I wasn't with you.

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:23.900
You understand?

00:26:28.180 --> 00:26:29.970
Remember, Julie, I wasn't...

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:59.960
with you. Thank you. Good. Good morning, Miss Danley. Good morning, Ann.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.860
I'll just have fruit juice, toast and coffee.

00:27:04.500 --> 00:27:06.060
I see my brother is having his troubles.

00:27:07.080 --> 00:27:09.320
Political opponents are after him like a pack of wolves.

00:27:09.480 --> 00:27:09.700
Really?

00:27:10.770 --> 00:27:13.490
Yes, they'd like nothing better than to find some chink in his armor.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:14.880
So far, they haven't had any luck.

00:27:15.660 --> 00:27:19.080
It'd be a great thing for the Caldwell family if the senator landed such an important position.

00:27:19.480 --> 00:27:20.700
It would make you world famous.

00:27:21.220 --> 00:27:23.760
Not that your scientific reputation isn't enough, of course.

00:27:24.710 --> 00:27:25.290
Hello, everybody.

00:27:25.570 --> 00:27:26.250
Morning, Julie.

00:27:26.590 --> 00:27:27.330
Good morning, Julie.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.460
I did not.

00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:35.130
You didn't? Why not?

00:27:36.860 --> 00:27:37.960
It happened again last night.

00:27:38.920 --> 00:27:39.240
What happened?

00:27:40.510 --> 00:27:41.390
Something woke me up.

00:27:42.530 --> 00:27:43.410
A sound of scuffling.

00:27:44.750 --> 00:27:46.170
It seemed to come from the laboratory.

00:27:47.550 --> 00:27:48.410
Somebody cried out.

00:27:49.230 --> 00:27:49.970
Oh, really, Julie?

00:27:50.130 --> 00:27:51.250
These nightmares of yours.

00:27:51.640 --> 00:27:53.360
You know perfectly well there's no one in that wing.

00:27:54.040 --> 00:27:54.940
It wasn't a nightmare.

00:27:55.320 --> 00:27:56.260
I heard it, I tell you.

00:27:56.720 --> 00:27:57.220
Couldn't have.

00:27:58.520 --> 00:27:59.380
Didn't you hear it, Sandra?

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:00.880
No, I'm afraid I didn't.

00:28:01.750 --> 00:28:05.450
Julie sometimes forgets that she's had dreams about my lab ever since she was a child.

00:28:06.130 --> 00:28:06.410
Why?

00:28:07.950 --> 00:28:10.110
Oh, I used to take her in there quite often when she was little.

00:28:11.620 --> 00:28:16.160
Then she'd start sneaking in when I wasn't there and playing around with the apparatus.

00:28:16.420 --> 00:28:17.260
And, of course, that was dangerous.

00:28:17.630 --> 00:28:19.010
So we had to put a lock on the place.

00:28:19.460 --> 00:28:20.480
I wasn't asleep.

00:28:21.130 --> 00:28:23.870
Don't you think if there had been some such noise, someone else would have heard it?

00:28:24.280 --> 00:28:25.000
Beckett, for instance.

00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:26.440
His rumors immediately...

00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:28.380
Beckett, he'd say anything you asked him to.

00:28:29.600 --> 00:28:29.960
That's...

00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:39.000
You're overly excited, my dear. You have a tendency that way, haven't you?

00:28:40.250 --> 00:28:41.090
May I make a suggestion?

00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:41.570
What?

00:28:42.330 --> 00:28:46.470
Next time you hear some odd noise in the night, just follow the memorable custom of your sex

00:28:46.470 --> 00:28:48.050
and stick your head under the bedclothes.

00:28:57.640 --> 00:28:58.640
See, he was lying.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:28:59.980
Yes, he was.

00:29:00.670 --> 00:29:01.470
What are we going to do?

00:29:01.880 --> 00:29:03.800
We mustn't do anything to make them suspicious.

00:29:04.500 --> 00:29:06.000
First of all, I want to see Jim's room.

00:29:06.710 --> 00:29:09.510
What is the schedule of the day here? Who is where, at what time?

00:29:10.090 --> 00:29:11.610
In the afternoon, Marta has her nap.

00:29:12.100 --> 00:29:14.040
Beckett keeps an eye on me then, but he has a lot to do.

00:29:15.130 --> 00:29:16.730
You won't keep me in the dark about things, will you?

00:29:16.930 --> 00:29:17.950
No, of course not, Julie.

00:29:18.190 --> 00:29:23.750
Good morning.

00:29:24.220 --> 00:29:24.440
Julie.

00:29:24.790 --> 00:29:25.150
Good morning.

00:29:35.120 --> 00:29:36.770
Let's go out to the garden.

00:29:46.080 --> 00:29:47.300
This is Jim's room.

00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:58.140
Look Sandra, these were all taken last summer. The girl there with him is Amy Daniels. That was about two years ago. Jim was awfully attractive, wasn't he? Yes.

00:31:01.690 --> 00:31:04.170
You know, there's something curious about this picture of Jim and Mark.

00:31:04.980 --> 00:31:05.480
What do you mean?

00:31:06.890 --> 00:31:08.190
Well, it's a friendly-looking picture.

00:31:09.150 --> 00:31:12.350
Not at all what I was led to believe about the way Jim and Mark got along.

00:31:13.100 --> 00:31:14.480
Mark used to be sweet to us.

00:31:15.450 --> 00:31:18.090
Perhaps it's because we were younger, more under his influence.

00:31:19.450 --> 00:31:21.710
It's only when we want to have our own way that he's mean.

00:31:30.190 --> 00:31:33.740
That was my mother. She died when I was four years old.

00:31:34.640 --> 00:31:35.980
Haven't you any pictures of your father?

00:31:37.330 --> 00:31:40.880
I can't even remember what he looked like. He died in a hospital.

00:31:42.650 --> 00:31:44.170
They say it broke my mother's heart.

00:31:55.730 --> 00:31:58.940
This money you are to inherit belonged to your mother, didn't it?

00:31:59.380 --> 00:31:59.620
Yes.

00:32:00.990 --> 00:32:03.110
She must have been very devoted to your Uncle Mark.

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:07.190
I know why you say that, on account of the will.

00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:09.460
Who's to know how devoted she was?

00:32:10.060 --> 00:32:12.060
I was only three when she and Mark drew it up.

00:32:12.280 --> 00:32:13.240
Jim was away at school.

00:32:14.550 --> 00:32:18.780
All I know is that my father was taken to a hospital, died there.

00:32:20.330 --> 00:32:21.890
And then our mother was never the same.

00:32:25.060 --> 00:32:29.280
Julie, is this the way Jim always kept his room?

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.240
Yes.

00:32:31.970 --> 00:32:33.590
Nothing's been changed or taken away?

00:32:35.080 --> 00:32:35.260
No.

00:32:36.500 --> 00:32:38.440
No, it's exactly the way it was when he was alive.

00:32:39.260 --> 00:32:40.760
I wonder why all his pipes are gone.

00:32:41.220 --> 00:32:42.180
Jim was always smoking.

00:32:45.580 --> 00:32:48.500
Yes, he had lots of pipes.

00:32:54.160 --> 00:32:55.140
Are these all his clothes?

00:32:58.250 --> 00:32:58.650
No.

00:32:59.530 --> 00:32:59.970
His sport...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:17.490
clothes are all gone the things he wore for riding for tennis sandra what does all this mean

00:33:17.490 --> 00:33:28.320
what are you thinking sandra you think it really was jim last night then what are they doing to him

00:33:28.890 --> 00:33:29.830
what's going on

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:30.580
I'm going to go to the laboratory.

00:33:31.040 --> 00:33:33.000
Sandra, tell me what's happening in there.

00:33:33.500 --> 00:33:34.220
Something horrible.

00:33:34.680 --> 00:33:36.260
That's why Mark won't let anybody in there.

00:33:36.660 --> 00:33:37.780
They'll take me next.

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:40.120
They won't let me off the estate.

00:33:40.630 --> 00:33:41.550
They won't get me.

00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:42.920
I'm going to run away.

00:33:43.450 --> 00:33:44.870
I won't stay in this awful place.

00:33:48.560 --> 00:33:50.110
They won't do anything to you.

00:33:50.190 --> 00:33:51.930
Now, please be sensible and calm, Daniel.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.320
Mr. Caldwell would like to see you in the library.

00:34:04.060 --> 00:34:05.180
Thank you. I'll be right down.

00:34:07.680 --> 00:34:09.060
Come on, Julie, I'll take you to your room.

00:34:25.510 --> 00:34:26.230
I'm afraid.

00:34:26.900 --> 00:34:28.360
I'm sorry I upset you.

00:34:28.720 --> 00:34:29.980
Please, lie down and get some room.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.830
I'll go and see what your Uncle Mark wants.

00:34:33.340 --> 00:34:34.000
You'll be all right?

00:34:35.370 --> 00:34:36.730
In this room, it isn't so bad.

00:34:38.220 --> 00:34:41.660
When the door's closed and I know that no one's looking at me.

00:34:43.520 --> 00:34:45.240
I don't like eyes looking at me.

00:34:46.280 --> 00:34:47.500
That's when I get frightened.

00:34:48.690 --> 00:34:51.810
Then I can't explain.

00:34:53.010 --> 00:34:54.910
It's as if everything went dark.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:57.520
As if something were closing in on me.

00:34:58.490 --> 00:34:59.370
A dark cloud.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.980
And I want to run and run and run, but he keeps following me.

00:35:03.640 --> 00:35:04.840
Then you mustn't run away.

00:35:05.440 --> 00:35:07.360
Turn around and face it. That's what I always do.

00:35:08.350 --> 00:35:10.410
But aren't you ever afraid?

00:35:11.300 --> 00:35:13.580
Oh, everyone's afraid. Once in a while, Julie did.

00:35:14.250 --> 00:35:17.110
For instance, a minute ago, I was afraid when I thought Jim was alive.

00:35:17.870 --> 00:35:20.530
I thought the way you did, that they were doing something awful to him.

00:35:21.280 --> 00:35:23.140
And do you see what happened? I made you afraid.

00:35:23.360 --> 00:35:26.890
And that was stupid. Fear is too...

00:35:30.860 --> 00:35:31.340
Okay.

00:35:31.600 --> 00:35:53.650
You wanted to see me?

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:56.300
Yes.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.240
Julie likes you, and I thought it'd be nice for her to have a companion.

00:36:04.270 --> 00:36:07.150
But I thought I'd also made it clear that she cannot be allowed to have her head.

00:36:08.110 --> 00:36:11.150
I'm told that you were both in Jim's room and that Julie was greatly upset.

00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:12.640
Yes, she was upset.

00:36:13.210 --> 00:36:16.790
Can't you see that dwelling on Jim is the worst possible thing you could do to Julie?

00:36:18.180 --> 00:36:21.870
I don't know what plans you have in that devious feminine mind of yours,

00:36:22.650 --> 00:36:26.050
but if you're trying to enlist Julie's sympathy, don't do it.

00:36:26.870 --> 00:36:28.250
And if I ignore your advice?

00:36:29.410 --> 00:36:29.970
I shall kick you up.

00:36:31.980 --> 00:36:34.620
That wouldn't do any good. Julie's very fond of me.

00:36:34.860 --> 00:36:38.800
I know. That's exactly why I've been so forbearing.

00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:43.160
So long as you're in this house, I'd like her to keep her illusions about you.

00:36:43.860 --> 00:36:45.460
She wouldn't have any if she knew why you were here.

00:36:46.430 --> 00:36:48.630
If I'm to believe you're acting in Julie's best interests,

00:36:49.160 --> 00:36:51.720
then you must believe I'm here because I have a right to be here.

00:36:52.530 --> 00:36:53.810
Of course, Mrs. Demarest.

00:36:54.690 --> 00:36:56.370
You're here because you're a member of the family.

00:36:57.160 --> 00:36:58.760
An unhappy bride of five months.

00:36:59.430 --> 00:36:59.970
In my opinion...

00:37:00.190 --> 00:37:01.050
You're wasting your time.

00:37:01.250 --> 00:37:03.730
Oh, don't forget, Mr. Caldwell, I have a card up my sleeve.

00:37:04.200 --> 00:37:06.940
A little matter of a will which your lawyer is attempting to find.

00:37:10.160 --> 00:37:12.580
I can assure you that if Davenport does find the will,

00:37:12.740 --> 00:37:14.180
I for one shall be vastly relieved.

00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:17.580
You know, the Caldwells have always been very proud of their women.

00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:19.940
No doubt you've noticed their portraits are around the walls.

00:37:21.250 --> 00:37:23.140
All of them beautiful, some of them clever.

00:37:24.360 --> 00:37:26.220
My grandfather, for instance, married a dancer.

00:37:27.100 --> 00:37:28.180
She was the toast of Paris.

00:37:28.870 --> 00:37:29.970
Doesn't sound like a Caldwell.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:37.400
Oh, he was a venturesome sort of father, sailed around the horn as a lad, kept him on a sailing ship, kept him a drink.

00:37:39.700 --> 00:37:42.300
Unfortunately, his romance for the dancer came to a bad end.

00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:42.940
Really?

00:37:43.890 --> 00:37:45.870
She died two months after they were married.

00:37:46.540 --> 00:37:47.080
What a pity.

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:48.820
He poisoned her.

00:37:52.230 --> 00:37:52.590
Wrong.

00:37:55.120 --> 00:37:59.140
Quite an interesting liqueur, isn't it?

00:38:00.380 --> 00:38:03.620
Made from a recipe belonging to our family and only used on special occasions.

00:38:04.120 --> 00:38:05.840
And you consider this a special occasion?

00:38:05.980 --> 00:38:06.720
I certainly do.

00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:08.800
Lovely color too, isn't it?

00:38:09.820 --> 00:38:10.880
And a fascinating name.

00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:12.380
Blackroma Sangui.

00:38:12.870 --> 00:38:13.490
Do you know Italian?

00:38:13.930 --> 00:38:15.650
Enough to know that it means tears of blood.

00:38:15.970 --> 00:38:16.810
Ah, yes, I forgot.

00:38:16.990 --> 00:38:17.370
Of course.

00:38:17.840 --> 00:38:19.060
You're a college graduate, aren't you?

00:38:19.960 --> 00:38:21.970
Well, to the will.

00:38:22.610 --> 00:38:23.510
Bless its little heart.

00:38:27.680 --> 00:38:28.220
Very good.

00:38:29.140 --> 00:38:29.440
Thank you.

00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:32.520
I'm glad to see you have an appreciation of good things.

00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:38.090
In fact, I'm beginning to realize it more and more.

00:38:38.870 --> 00:38:40.710
You're altogether a very charming person.

00:38:42.770 --> 00:38:43.230
Thank you.

00:38:43.630 --> 00:38:44.030
Attractive.

00:38:45.040 --> 00:38:47.820
I like women with steady eyes, firm chin.

00:38:48.340 --> 00:38:50.060
My teeth are also very good.

00:38:50.780 --> 00:38:52.280
And, of course, a sense of humor.

00:38:52.540 --> 00:38:53.520
What am I supposed to do?

00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:55.720
Turn this into a mutual admiration society?

00:38:55.920 --> 00:38:56.600
Oh, no, no.

00:38:56.800 --> 00:38:59.880
I think it's a little late for you to change your first impression of me.

00:39:00.570 --> 00:39:01.510
You don't like me, do you?

00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:06.360
Hmm. Silence is revealing.

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:08.440
I'm the silent type.

00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:11.000
I wonder what type you really are.

00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:13.820
Oh, surely your scientific mind has figured that out by now.

00:39:14.460 --> 00:39:16.640
It would be interesting to know into which category I fall.

00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:17.240
Category?

00:39:17.520 --> 00:39:17.780
Yes.

00:39:18.410 --> 00:39:23.210
Don't you catalogue all women and keep them neatly filed in a sort of mental card index?

00:39:23.710 --> 00:39:24.050
No.

00:39:24.870 --> 00:39:27.150
No, in my human relations, I'm quite open-minded.

00:39:27.780 --> 00:39:28.540
You've surprised me.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:30.800
And I am progressing.

00:39:33.180 --> 00:39:36.380
Yes. I think it's time I got dressed for dinner.

00:39:36.890 --> 00:39:38.670
By dinner time, we'll be right back where we started.

00:39:40.320 --> 00:39:41.580
You underestimate yourself.

00:39:42.540 --> 00:39:43.700
Oh, then I have made an impression.

00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:44.880
A good one, I hope.

00:39:45.910 --> 00:39:46.530
No, don't answer.

00:39:46.780 --> 00:39:47.920
Just let me use my imagination.

00:39:48.990 --> 00:39:49.790
Can I trust it?

00:39:50.690 --> 00:39:51.850
Not to carry me too far.

00:39:53.060 --> 00:39:54.740
Might sooner not commit myself.

00:39:54.940 --> 00:39:56.180
I'd prefer to give it free reign.

00:39:57.550 --> 00:39:59.810
I'd like to probe behind that sphinx-like exterior.

00:40:01.190 --> 00:40:03.390
Find out what goes on behind those eyes.

00:40:06.890 --> 00:40:08.030
Very lovely eyes.

00:40:24.910 --> 00:40:25.750
Why did you do that?

00:40:26.650 --> 00:40:28.370
The scientist in me came uppermost.

00:40:30.920 --> 00:40:31.540
Scientist?

00:40:32.540 --> 00:40:33.800
Yes, purely research.

00:40:35.400 --> 00:40:37.760
I wanted to confirm my first impression of you.

00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:40.080
And did you?

00:40:40.440 --> 00:40:40.880
I did.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:03.800
Dearest, Miss Julie would like to know if she could borrow your cold cream.

00:41:04.060 --> 00:41:18.140
Certainly, Angela. Miss Julie, have a rest.

00:41:18.370 --> 00:41:19.740
Oh, yes, ma'am. Thank you.

00:41:52.780 --> 00:41:54.800
Just doing what I'm told, Miss Judy.

00:42:31.150 --> 00:42:33.050
Oh, Mrs. Demarest, I've been meaning to ask you,

00:42:33.210 --> 00:42:35.190
would you like some hot chocolate before you go to bed?

00:42:35.550 --> 00:42:37.570
Well, now that you've mentioned it, sounds very nice.

00:42:37.730 --> 00:42:40.030
Oh, I'm awfully sorry. You could have had it last night.

00:42:40.270 --> 00:42:42.650
I'm new here and it takes a while to get used to things.

00:42:42.830 --> 00:42:44.010
You sure it's not too much trouble?

00:42:44.210 --> 00:42:44.790
Oh, no.

00:42:45.390 --> 00:42:47.110
Now, Miss Julie always has hot chocolate

00:42:47.110 --> 00:42:50.330
and Mr. Caldwell, his sandwiches and scotch in the laboratory.

00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:54.860
Must be quite a problem to get anything to Mr. Caldwell

00:42:54.860 --> 00:42:56.860
way off there, sealed up in this lab.

00:42:57.180 --> 00:42:59.040
Oh, Beckett always fixes his tray for him.

00:42:59.280 --> 00:42:59.980
It goes up in the...

00:43:00.400 --> 00:43:05.260
Of course nobody else does it. Mr. Mark is so particular about the laboratory.

00:43:06.400 --> 00:43:09.000
I guess he does need something working so late.

00:43:09.800 --> 00:43:11.740
Well, sometimes he works as late as 2 o'clock.

00:43:13.170 --> 00:43:14.770
And sometimes all night I wager.

00:43:15.070 --> 00:43:18.360
Oh, no, ma'am. No, he has very regular habits. It's never later than 2.

00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:22.170
He's sort of particular about that. He likes us to be regular, too.

00:43:22.590 --> 00:43:24.870
For instance, Beckett always sends the tray up at 12.

00:43:25.610 --> 00:43:29.970
Once it was 12.30 and Mr. Mark didn't like it. Well...

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.780
I'll bring your hot chocolate in just a few minutes.

00:43:32.670 --> 00:43:33.350
Thank you, Angela.

00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:02.700
Thank you.

00:45:35.630 --> 00:45:37.950
You mustn't come here again unless I tell you who's dead.

00:45:38.250 --> 00:45:38.510
Yes, sir.

00:45:39.470 --> 00:45:41.120
Well, is everything all right at Three Hills?

00:45:41.680 --> 00:45:44.080
Yes, sir, but I wish you could come out there sometimes.

00:45:44.940 --> 00:45:45.460
It's impossible.

00:45:46.670 --> 00:45:47.670
You mean on account of that girl?

00:45:48.520 --> 00:45:49.040
Who is she?

00:45:50.350 --> 00:45:51.410
Claims to be Jim's wife.

00:45:52.260 --> 00:45:53.010
Jim's wife?

00:45:54.380 --> 00:45:55.460
We're checking our story.

00:45:56.110 --> 00:45:59.100
Well, in the meantime, if she should find out anything, I'd...

00:45:59.100 --> 00:45:59.840
That's my problem.

00:46:01.720 --> 00:46:03.700
That prescription you wanted's in the filing cabinet.

00:46:05.680 --> 00:46:06.380
I'll get it by here.

00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:11.020
I'm getting kind of worried about the prescription, Mr. Mark.

00:46:11.520 --> 00:46:13.760
I don't like the idea of having it filled around here.

00:46:14.210 --> 00:46:16.210
You know how the gossips are at the drugstore.

00:46:16.330 --> 00:46:17.690
Everybody knows everybody else's business.

00:46:18.150 --> 00:46:19.730
Then take it into Salem and have it filled.

00:46:19.870 --> 00:46:20.710
Good heavens, Liddell.

00:46:20.830 --> 00:46:22.690
Use your head. Don't bother me with details.

00:46:22.970 --> 00:46:24.390
You sure Doc Reynolds is all right?

00:46:24.850 --> 00:46:26.790
Reynolds is an old and valued family friend.

00:46:26.930 --> 00:46:28.470
As well as being a doctor, I'll take care of him.

00:46:28.810 --> 00:46:29.970
I'm not suggesting you're not...

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.920
I'm doing your part, Mr. Mark. Don't get me wrong.

00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:33.300
Then stop talking nonsense.

00:46:33.640 --> 00:46:39.040
I don't remember sending that traitor.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:00.500
No.

00:49:06.556 --> 00:49:06.916
an accident.

00:49:07.228 --> 00:49:08.428
She was trying to run away.

00:49:08.588 --> 00:49:09.228
That's a lie.

00:49:09.692 --> 00:49:10.452
It was an accident.

00:49:10.632 --> 00:49:12.132
That's a lie. That's a lie.

00:49:34.890 --> 00:49:35.230
This way, Doc.

00:49:47.520 --> 00:49:50.880
I'll have to notify the coroner. That's the law in case of violent death.

00:49:55.280 --> 00:49:58.970
If she was trying to run away, she wouldn't have taken this. It's mine.

00:50:00.508 --> 00:50:01.508
Someone else packed it.

00:50:02.652 --> 00:50:04.652
Someone who does what you tell her to do.

00:50:14.940 --> 00:50:15.240
Top.

00:50:15.324 --> 00:50:16.444
that Angela.

00:50:17.788 --> 00:50:19.788
I'll never forgive myself.

00:50:19.868 --> 00:50:20.868
Never.

00:50:21.532 --> 00:50:23.532
Being asleep last night when it happens.

00:50:24.220 --> 00:50:25.200
Maybe, but...

00:50:25.216 --> 00:50:29.236
If I'd been awake, I might have heard something and stopped her some way.

00:50:30.668 --> 00:50:34.268
Nobody could have done anything last night. It happened too quickly.

00:50:34.348 --> 00:50:35.708
Come, we're finished in here.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:00.600
Three, heel.

00:54:01.820 --> 00:54:03.900
Do you have any explanation for your remarkable behavior?

00:54:05.130 --> 00:54:07.050
What is this insane desire to get into my lab?

00:54:07.170 --> 00:54:08.010
I want to find Jim.

00:54:10.410 --> 00:54:12.970
And what makes you think Jim has risen from the dead?

00:54:13.070 --> 00:54:14.070
I don't think he is dead.

00:54:16.410 --> 00:54:17.530
You are a remarkable woman.

00:54:17.690 --> 00:54:19.590
You fling the most amazing accusations at me,

00:54:19.770 --> 00:54:20.890
without proof of any kind.

00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:23.370
Or do you think you have some proof?

00:54:24.620 --> 00:54:24.960
Maybe.

00:54:26.200 --> 00:54:27.760
Don't try my patience too far.

00:54:28.420 --> 00:54:28.940
What do you know?

00:54:29.080 --> 00:54:29.960
Or what do you think you know?

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:33.500
I don't know what you've done to Jim or where he is, but I do know what happened to Julie.

00:54:33.600 --> 00:54:36.000
You may not have killed her with your own hands, but you drove her to her death.

00:54:36.100 --> 00:54:38.000
How dare you say that? It was an accident.

00:54:38.100 --> 00:54:40.000
She must have been trying to climb down the trellis and slip.

00:54:40.100 --> 00:54:40.700
I don't believe it.

00:54:40.800 --> 00:54:42.500
I don't give a hoot and Hades what you believe.

00:54:43.660 --> 00:54:44.700
I warned you about, Julie.

00:54:45.228 --> 00:54:46.648
You ignored my advice.

00:54:46.732 --> 00:54:48.732
Filling her head with stupid ideas about me.

00:54:48.732 --> 00:54:50.732
Oh, don't deny it, Ma, I heard you.

00:54:50.892 --> 00:54:51.852
You made her afraid.

00:54:52.204 --> 00:54:54.984
so that the poor kid tried to run away from the home when she'd been sheltered, loved.

00:54:55.024 --> 00:54:56.804
If you loved her so much, why did you keep her a prisoner?

00:54:56.844 --> 00:54:58.064
I thought it best for her.

00:54:58.860 --> 00:55:00.000
It was until you came.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:03.490
She didn't think so. The very first night I arrived she came to my room.

00:55:03.530 --> 00:55:06.630
She talked about you and your treatment of Jim. There's something else you should know.

00:55:07.150 --> 00:55:12.170
Everything she said that morning at breakfast about hearing a man's voice screams was all true.

00:55:12.330 --> 00:55:14.680
I know because I heard it too.

00:55:15.990 --> 00:55:17.510
She was with me. We heard it together.

00:55:17.690 --> 00:55:19.260
She was with you?

00:55:19.280 --> 00:55:19.960
In my room.

00:55:20.200 --> 00:55:22.360
We knew you were lying.

00:55:22.580 --> 00:55:23.820
I see.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:27.130
To what use do you intend putting this knowledge?

00:55:28.860 --> 00:55:29.260
Well...

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.300
What are you going to do?

00:55:31.916 --> 00:55:32.416
Answer me!

00:55:33.004 --> 00:55:35.004
You

00:55:37.356 --> 00:55:38.196
I think.

00:55:38.604 --> 00:55:40.604
leave.

00:55:42.316 --> 00:55:43.156
All right.

00:55:46.796 --> 00:55:47.296
prefer that

00:55:49.964 --> 00:55:51.424
Here's something else you might need.

00:55:58.028 --> 00:55:58.868
All right.

00:55:59.468 --> 00:55:59.968
Ashes.

00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:07.240
to ashes, dust to dust, ensure uncertain hope of the resurrection unto eternal life

00:56:07.240 --> 00:56:14.240
through our Lord Jesus Christ, at whose coming in glorious majesty to judge the world, the

00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:19.400
earth and the sea shall give up their dead, and the corruptible bodies of those who sleep

00:56:19.400 --> 00:56:24.750
in him shall be changed and made like unto his own glorious body.

00:56:36.040 --> 00:56:38.330
Martha, you'll all be leaving on tonight's train.

00:56:38.470 --> 00:56:38.830
Yes, sir.

00:56:39.210 --> 00:56:40.910
I'll be driving so you can take my things with you.

00:56:41.740 --> 00:56:43.400
And you might just pack me an overnight bag, will you?

00:56:43.580 --> 00:56:44.020
Yes, sir.

00:57:01.920 --> 00:57:07.790
The last time of anything is sad, but sometimes I think not knowing it is the last time is even worse.

00:57:09.970 --> 00:57:12.210
I was thinking of that ride Julie and I took together.

00:57:13.990 --> 00:57:18.640
She had known how she would have drained every last moment of its happiness.

00:57:27.380 --> 00:57:29.970
At least I've left this room alone.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:46.790
until we left believe it but this was once a very happy house jim and julie were kids

00:57:46.790 --> 00:57:57.310
one summer fourth of july i think it was invited everybody for miles around to come and celebrate

00:57:57.310 --> 00:57:59.970
and bring their kids julie had a small

00:58:00.060 --> 00:58:03.310
She was an old pony then. She must have been about five or six, I guess.

00:58:04.120 --> 00:58:09.880
She was giving the other kids rides. One little guy got bucked off into the fish pond.

00:58:10.580 --> 00:58:14.080
She laughed so hard at the sight of that kid standing shivering there in his wet things

00:58:14.080 --> 00:58:18.640
that all the other kids started jumping in, too, just to hear her laugh some more.

00:58:19.440 --> 00:58:23.800
It's the effect her laugh to head on you, but to hear it again and again.

00:58:25.470 --> 00:58:26.910
Oh, something I'd like to show you.

00:58:41.770 --> 00:58:44.210
Most people don't appreciate fine old pieces like this.

00:58:45.710 --> 00:58:46.570
Thought perhaps you might.

00:58:48.940 --> 00:58:50.760
My father's wedding present to my mother.

00:58:52.720 --> 00:58:54.680
And this was given to my sister when Jim was born.

00:58:55.740 --> 00:58:57.020
No jewels, quite like a pearl.

00:58:57.280 --> 00:58:59.740
It's like the ocean they come from, same.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:04.860
The same depth, the same coldness, the same subtle cruelty just beneath the surface.

00:59:06.830 --> 00:59:09.290
And this my brother and I gave her when Julie was born.

00:59:10.370 --> 00:59:11.650
That was a great event for us, a girl.

00:59:11.960 --> 00:59:13.320
The cold rules generally around the boys.

00:59:14.240 --> 00:59:16.840
These were all meant for Julie when she grew old enough to appreciate them.

00:59:17.610 --> 00:59:18.630
I'd like you to take what you want.

00:59:20.980 --> 00:59:21.360
Why me?

00:59:22.250 --> 00:59:22.970
You're Jim's widow.

00:59:28.050 --> 00:59:29.570
Change your mind about me, haven't you?

00:59:30.440 --> 00:59:32.280
I spoke to Davenport on the telephone this morning.

00:59:33.650 --> 00:59:35.450
Jim's safety deposit box has been found.

00:59:36.130 --> 00:59:36.550
I see.

00:59:37.280 --> 00:59:38.340
It was opened by court order.

00:59:38.700 --> 00:59:40.150
The will was in it, completely attested.

00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:43.540
A little late for apologies.

00:59:43.740 --> 00:59:44.820
Things have gone too far for that.

00:59:45.980 --> 00:59:46.840
I'm leaving for Washington.

00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:49.980
You're more than welcome to stay in the Boston house as long as you want.

00:59:50.980 --> 00:59:53.600
I can't understand why you want me around after what's happened.

00:59:55.870 --> 00:59:56.990
Tragedy strikes a house.

00:59:57.930 --> 00:59:59.680
The lives of everyone in it come.

01:00:00.030 --> 01:00:11.370
tangled up don't you think what are you going to do i haven't decided yet you know i really am very

01:00:11.370 --> 01:00:17.620
sorry for having treated you the way i have thank you and there's something else come with me will you

01:00:17.620 --> 01:00:29.190
where are we going to my lab

01:00:30.190 --> 01:00:31.670
You always wanted to get in there, didn't you?

01:00:32.450 --> 01:00:33.710
Well, I did, but now...

01:00:33.710 --> 01:00:36.870
Oh, come now. At least give me a chance to change your opinion of me.

01:00:37.070 --> 01:00:37.970
Why do you bother?

01:00:38.680 --> 01:00:41.200
I wouldn't like you to leave this house thinking badly of me.

01:00:42.000 --> 01:00:46.410
What makes you think showing me an empty room will change my opinion of you?

01:00:46.720 --> 01:00:47.460
It'll be a beginning.

01:00:48.060 --> 01:00:48.560
Of what?

01:00:49.940 --> 01:00:53.450
Somehow, you and I seem to have built a wall between us.

01:00:54.510 --> 01:00:55.770
I'd like to try to break it down.

01:00:56.480 --> 01:00:58.220
See, Sandra.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.770
I find I like you very much, very much indeed.

01:01:04.150 --> 01:01:05.970
What is this, more scientific research?

01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:09.640
Very easily, do you?

01:01:09.820 --> 01:01:10.100
No.

01:01:11.570 --> 01:01:12.470
No, I don't forget.

01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:27.000
This room I think you know.

01:02:00.960 --> 01:02:06.280
Simple workroom, hidden secrets, no mysterious strangers.

01:02:12.100 --> 01:02:12.800
Who is Lydell?

01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:18.560
Lydell, sort of gamekeeper.

01:02:19.890 --> 01:02:20.950
Been with you a long time?

01:02:21.570 --> 01:02:22.090
Quite long.

01:02:24.680 --> 01:02:28.060
Like Dr. Reynolds, an old and trusted friend, as well as a servant?

01:02:29.290 --> 01:02:29.670
That's right.

01:02:31.080 --> 01:02:32.800
Must be wonderful to command such loyalty.

01:02:33.680 --> 01:02:34.220
It is.

01:02:37.930 --> 01:02:39.030
How can you give it all up?

01:02:39.890 --> 01:02:42.830
Go and live in an apartment in Washington, leave this house, this estate.

01:02:44.420 --> 01:02:45.560
I couldn't work here anymore.

01:02:46.750 --> 01:02:48.010
There's too many unhappy memories.

01:02:50.610 --> 01:02:51.810
What are you doing about the horses?

01:02:56.330 --> 01:02:57.010
Have they gone yet?

01:02:58.040 --> 01:02:58.300
Why?

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:29.750
like to ride, do you mind? Of course not. Nothing to do until we leave tonight. I'll call down the stables. Damaris is going riding.

01:03:30.790 --> 01:03:32.700
Yes, let her have a colonel, will you?

01:03:32.780 --> 01:03:41.740
Good afternoon, Mrs. Demarest.

01:03:42.060 --> 01:03:43.100
Well, there he is already.

01:03:43.360 --> 01:03:44.780
Thanks, Roberts, I shan't be long.

01:03:45.100 --> 01:03:45.600
No, ma'am.

01:03:46.670 --> 01:03:49.010
What are you going to do now that the house is being closed up?

01:03:49.280 --> 01:03:50.680
I got a job at the Mannings, ma'am.

01:03:51.600 --> 01:03:52.720
Have you been here a long time?

01:03:53.640 --> 01:03:55.360
About five years before the war.

01:03:56.220 --> 01:03:58.680
Oh, were you in the service?

01:03:59.050 --> 01:03:59.670
Yes, ma'am.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.160
Canadian Air Force, two years overseas.

01:04:03.780 --> 01:04:05.820
Well, there he is, he needs some exercise.

01:04:07.180 --> 01:04:08.620
The good horse he is, I'll miss him.

01:04:11.670 --> 01:04:13.030
I don't want to ride off the estate.

01:04:13.370 --> 01:04:14.950
How far does it extend exactly?

01:04:15.390 --> 01:04:18.780
Well, you go down the road as far as that there other gate,

01:04:18.900 --> 01:04:20.240
the one they never use no more,

01:04:20.980 --> 01:04:23.840
and back into the woods, way back as far as them three hills.

01:04:25.690 --> 01:04:26.370
The three hills?

01:04:26.760 --> 01:04:27.780
That's the game preserve.

01:04:28.100 --> 01:04:29.980
It's a lonely sort of a place no one ever goes to.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:35.880
there no more is there a lodge there or anything yes ma'am never used no more if you think in the

01:04:35.880 --> 01:04:42.400
riding over that way i shouldn't if i was you it's kind of overgrown don't worry i won't no good ride

01:05:30.030 --> 01:05:30.390
Thank you.

01:08:10.910 --> 01:08:11.330
I'm coming.

01:08:32.590 --> 01:08:45.860
Jim, Jim, I've been searching for you everywhere, ever since I came to Willow Miles.

01:08:46.120 --> 01:08:46.760
Willow Miles?

01:08:47.970 --> 01:08:48.970
Jim, don't you remember me?

01:08:50.830 --> 01:08:53.850
It's so difficult to remember. It's been difficult ever since the accident.

01:08:55.210 --> 01:08:55.790
What accident?

01:08:56.730 --> 01:08:59.630
I'll be all right. I'm going to stay here until I'm well.

01:09:00.440 --> 01:09:01.560
Well, I'd always take care of me.

01:09:03.070 --> 01:09:04.190
What do you mean, take care of you?

01:09:04.890 --> 01:09:06.450
They give me things to make me sleep.

01:09:06.650 --> 01:09:07.990
If they didn't, I wouldn't be able to.

01:09:10.960 --> 01:09:11.880
Jim, listen to me.

01:09:12.620 --> 01:09:16.240
Don't you remember the things you told me about Mark trying to get your money away from you?

01:09:16.760 --> 01:09:19.300
That's why we were married, so you could stop him from getting him.

01:09:19.650 --> 01:09:20.690
Surely you remember that.

01:09:21.650 --> 01:09:22.610
Mark sent me here.

01:09:25.440 --> 01:09:27.860
Told me you thought he was planning to murder you.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:32.300
Sandra, I remember you.

01:09:32.740 --> 01:09:35.050
Jim, last week there was a funeral.

01:09:35.520 --> 01:09:36.400
It was a mock funeral.

01:09:36.520 --> 01:09:37.320
People think you're dead.

01:09:37.540 --> 01:09:38.300
Mark arranged it.

01:09:38.380 --> 01:09:39.220
Don't lie to me, Sandra.

01:09:39.300 --> 01:09:39.900
It's the truth.

01:09:40.100 --> 01:09:41.420
Why should Mark do a thing like that?

01:09:41.560 --> 01:09:43.840
He has control of your money now, and Julie's too.

01:09:44.080 --> 01:09:45.460
Julie's too young to get in his way.

01:09:45.520 --> 01:09:46.200
He won't hurt her.

01:09:48.240 --> 01:09:50.530
Jim, Julie is dead.

01:09:51.060 --> 01:09:51.360
Julie?

01:09:51.600 --> 01:09:52.720
She was driven to her death.

01:09:52.920 --> 01:09:53.440
Mark did it.

01:09:55.850 --> 01:09:56.450
Say Mark did it?

01:09:56.510 --> 01:09:57.150
Yes, yes.

01:09:57.270 --> 01:09:59.530
Now he has all the money, just as you were afraid of.

01:10:00.090 --> 01:10:00.910
Yes, I was afraid of that.

01:10:01.110 --> 01:10:02.450
He's closing up the house, going away.

01:10:02.590 --> 01:10:04.690
For the rest of your life, no one must know that you're alive.

01:10:04.830 --> 01:10:05.970
Don't you understand, Jim?

01:10:06.530 --> 01:10:07.390
But you know, Sandra.

01:10:08.030 --> 01:10:08.770
Yes, I know.

01:10:09.940 --> 01:10:13.340
And he can't close my mouth with money the way he did the undertaker and the doctor.

01:10:13.500 --> 01:10:14.580
But he can close your mouth.

01:10:14.640 --> 01:10:15.580
He wouldn't dare.

01:10:15.600 --> 01:10:16.280
He'll dare anything.

01:10:18.970 --> 01:10:19.450
What was that?

01:10:20.080 --> 01:10:20.400
Liddell.

01:10:20.940 --> 01:10:21.980
Jim, supper's ready.

01:10:22.340 --> 01:10:22.660
Coming!

01:10:23.120 --> 01:10:28.060
Now listen to me.

01:10:28.300 --> 01:10:28.860
You do what I say.

01:10:28.920 --> 01:10:29.640
You go back to the house.

01:10:30.410 --> 01:10:31.610
I'll have to wait till they think I'm asleep.

01:10:32.090 --> 01:10:32.450
But Jim...

01:10:32.450 --> 01:10:33.270
Now don't worry.

01:10:33.900 --> 01:10:35.460
When they give me my sleeping pills, I'll cool them.

01:10:35.660 --> 01:10:36.920
After they're asleep, I'll get out of here.

01:10:38.260 --> 01:10:39.760
Take it easy, Lydell. I'm coming.

01:10:45.660 --> 01:10:46.440
Check this path here.

01:10:46.560 --> 01:10:48.020
It leads around behind the shed where they keep the truck.

01:10:48.380 --> 01:10:49.880
Keep it among the trees till you get to the gate.

01:10:50.610 --> 01:10:52.230
Mrs. Lydell's gone into town for supplies.

01:10:52.370 --> 01:10:53.250
She'll be coming back with the truck.

01:10:53.660 --> 01:10:54.900
While she's driving through the gate,

01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:56.340
you'll have to slip through before she locks it.

01:10:57.110 --> 01:10:57.630
Do you think you can do that?

01:10:57.710 --> 01:10:58.990
Yes, but how are you going to get out?

01:10:59.270 --> 01:10:59.970
I'll meet you at the house.

01:11:01.150 --> 01:11:04.500
Oh, don't worry. They both sleep like logs. Watch yourself.

01:11:04.980 --> 01:11:07.480
Jim! Jim, what's going on?

01:11:07.740 --> 01:11:09.920
You're like an old hen, Lydell. Here I am.

01:11:12.240 --> 01:11:13.400
I've had some cards after dinner.

01:11:15.280 --> 01:11:17.950
Why, sure. Sure, Jim. Anything you say.

01:13:15.480 --> 01:13:15.960
I was thrown.

01:13:16.240 --> 01:13:17.640
Oh, I thought you must have been.

01:13:17.780 --> 01:13:20.300
When the horse came back without you, we've been searching for you for hours.

01:13:20.730 --> 01:13:21.230
I'm sorry.

01:13:21.490 --> 01:13:22.440
Oh, that's all right.

01:13:22.540 --> 01:13:23.740
It's lucky you weren't hurt.

01:13:23.860 --> 01:13:25.870
I kept a fire going for you in the library.

01:13:25.950 --> 01:13:26.290
Come on in.

01:13:30.440 --> 01:13:32.040
You must have ridden quite a long way.

01:13:32.640 --> 01:13:32.960
Yes.

01:13:33.200 --> 01:13:35.060
How far?

01:13:35.810 --> 01:13:36.510
Oh, I don't know.

01:13:36.550 --> 01:13:36.950
Through the woods.

01:13:36.990 --> 01:13:37.770
I can't tell exactly.

01:13:48.870 --> 01:13:51.620
Roberts, it's all right. Mrs. Damarest is back.

01:13:52.790 --> 01:13:57.720
Yes. Well, I won't see you again, so goodbye and thank you.

01:14:01.564 --> 01:14:03.904
Well, it's too late for the train, so you'll have to drive in with me.

01:14:05.052 --> 01:14:07.052
I had Ma to leave you a tray. Won't you have something to eat?

01:14:07.052 --> 01:14:09.052
No, thank you. I'm not hungry.

01:14:09.148 --> 01:14:11.148
Well, I suppose the sooner we get going the better.

01:14:11.148 --> 01:14:13.448
Would you mind very much if I stayed here tonight?

01:14:13.596 --> 01:14:16.016
I'll get a taxi to take me to the station in the morning.

01:14:17.340 --> 01:14:18.700
The house is closed. There's no one here.

01:14:19.484 --> 01:14:20.504
I can manage.

01:14:21.052 --> 01:14:22.472
Well, in that case, I'll stay on, too.

01:14:22.672 --> 01:14:25.032
Oh, no, I wouldn't want you to change your plans on my account.

01:14:26.140 --> 01:14:27.360
Well, that's all right. I prefer it.

01:14:27.900 --> 01:14:29.500
As a matter of fact, I don't like driving at night either.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:32.680
No, I'll be all right, really. Won't you please...

01:14:32.680 --> 01:14:34.680
You're not trying to drive me out of my own house, are you?

01:14:34.720 --> 01:14:37.440
Of course not.

01:14:45.220 --> 01:14:54.560
Look Sandra, you and I may never see each other again. So there's something I should tell you.

01:14:55.060 --> 01:14:59.020
I think I will have something to eat after all. I'll take it up to my room.

01:15:07.356 --> 01:15:08.676
Why don't you just have it by the fire?

01:15:09.244 --> 01:15:10.384
I'll see you in the morning. Good night.

01:16:02.140 --> 01:16:05.820
think you're doing let me go not until you explain yourself what made you think i was jim

01:16:05.820 --> 01:16:13.520
i didn't i you still think he's alive don't you yes i do i don't know who or what was in the coffin

01:16:13.520 --> 01:16:21.510
that day but i do know that jim is alive i've seen him i've spoken to him you want the truth

01:16:21.510 --> 01:16:27.100
you'll have it try to tell you inside but you wouldn't listen you're not going to like it

01:16:27.100 --> 01:16:29.910
it was a very good

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:32.540
There's no reason for the will that made me trustee for Jim and Julie.

01:16:33.670 --> 01:16:37.960
Their father died in a sanitarium, violently insane.

01:16:41.870 --> 01:16:46.160
The father was in... no.

01:16:48.570 --> 01:16:48.730
No.

01:16:49.190 --> 01:16:50.150
There's proof in my safe.

01:16:52.740 --> 01:16:57.840
I wonder if you have any idea what it is to live in the shadow of insanity.

01:17:00.600 --> 01:17:04.840
If you had, you could understand a lot of things.

01:17:07.710 --> 01:17:10.030
Ever since they were children, I had to take care of them, watch them.

01:17:10.470 --> 01:17:12.750
For any sign of that terrible thing that I knew was in their blood.

01:17:14.210 --> 01:17:17.210
I took them to the finest psychiatrists, the finest doctors in the world.

01:17:17.310 --> 01:17:20.740
They could do nothing. All they did was tell me to watch them.

01:17:21.920 --> 01:17:25.200
Watch them carefully. I did my best.

01:17:26.280 --> 01:17:29.840
If you are telling the truth, it really happened to Julie.

01:17:31.720 --> 01:17:32.560
I can only give you an opinion.

01:17:34.630 --> 01:17:35.530
No one was in the room with her.

01:17:36.080 --> 01:17:36.800
No one spoke to her.

01:17:38.680 --> 01:17:40.510
I think Julie knew about herself.

01:17:42.270 --> 01:17:43.430
I believe she committed suicide.

01:17:44.070 --> 01:17:45.930
Then why did you try to make it look like an accident?

01:17:46.400 --> 01:17:46.920
I had to.

01:17:47.330 --> 01:17:49.980
Because of my brother.

01:17:51.750 --> 01:17:53.310
If his enemies, and he has plenty of them,

01:17:53.600 --> 01:17:55.260
ever knew that a member of the Caldwell family

01:17:55.260 --> 01:17:56.120
had committed suicide,

01:17:56.240 --> 01:17:57.580
that there was insanity in the family.

01:17:57.870 --> 01:17:59.970
But you said the insanity is in the Demarest place.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:04.870
Do you think that would have stopped them? They would have crucified him. I had to protect him.

01:18:05.010 --> 01:18:06.770
Why do you keep Jim a prisoner in that place?

01:18:08.080 --> 01:18:08.960
Jim killed a man.

01:18:13.420 --> 01:18:14.220
I don't believe it.

01:18:14.660 --> 01:18:16.740
Don't you? You're going to listen anyway.

01:18:17.850 --> 01:18:21.470
He was on a vacation in Canada. Must have been shortly after you were married, I imagine.

01:18:22.180 --> 01:18:23.840
Car skidded. It was an accident.

01:18:24.730 --> 01:18:26.570
He got into an argument with a gas station attendant.

01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:29.360
Hit the man with a wrench. He died the next day.

01:18:30.920 --> 01:18:35.320
I did everything I could, used every bit of influence my brother and I had to keep it out of the American papers.

01:18:36.600 --> 01:18:40.480
The upshot of it was, court committed him to my care.

01:18:41.380 --> 01:18:43.440
Rigid confinement for the rest of his life.

01:18:44.810 --> 01:18:46.430
Most of the time, of course, he's quite normal.

01:18:47.360 --> 01:18:49.780
Then something happens that upsets him and he goes berserk.

01:18:50.700 --> 01:18:51.720
That's what you heard the other night.

01:18:51.820 --> 01:18:53.800
I had to keep him in that wing until I had the compound ready.

01:18:55.400 --> 01:18:59.980
Now perhaps you can imagine how I felt when you suddenly appeared and claimed to be his...

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:04.160
I'd been warned that under no circumstances could either of them,

01:19:04.240 --> 01:19:06.240
Jim or Julie, ever marry, have children.

01:19:10.980 --> 01:19:15.450
But it can't be true. I've seen Jim. I've talked to him.

01:19:17.090 --> 01:19:18.750
He's as normal as you or I.

01:19:33.930 --> 01:19:35.490
He's telling you a lot of lies about me and you believed him.

01:19:35.590 --> 01:19:38.210
No, I didn't, but you shouldn't have done this. You might have killed him.

01:19:38.310 --> 01:19:39.350
What if I did? Would it make any difference?

01:19:41.570 --> 01:19:42.350
Are you in love with him?

01:19:43.190 --> 01:19:44.810
No, Jim, of course not, but I...

01:19:44.810 --> 01:19:52.970
In love with him?

01:19:53.950 --> 01:19:54.690
Let me go.

01:19:54.910 --> 01:19:55.890
No, you're going away with me.

01:19:56.920 --> 01:19:58.200
First, I want to destroy those papers.

01:19:59.460 --> 01:19:59.740
Papers?

01:20:00.120 --> 01:20:01.900
I heard what Mark was telling you. I can open a safe.

01:20:02.220 --> 01:20:03.320
I don't want there to be any proof.

01:20:04.070 --> 01:20:05.110
Proof of anything.

01:20:06.720 --> 01:20:07.980
We'll get in the car and go away.

01:20:09.440 --> 01:20:11.620
You do want to go away with me, don't you, Sandra?

01:20:13.500 --> 01:20:28.980
Do, Sandra.

01:20:34.540 --> 01:20:35.400
I've never hurt anybody.

01:20:36.340 --> 01:20:49.830
You put me away again, don't you?

01:20:49.890 --> 01:20:51.270
But you're not, because you won't get the chance.

01:20:51.510 --> 01:20:53.330
I don't want you to go back to that place, don't you remember?

01:20:53.390 --> 01:20:54.610
I begged you to come with me.

01:20:54.710 --> 01:20:55.840
You think I'm crazy?

01:20:56.500 --> 01:20:56.960
I'm not.

01:20:57.040 --> 01:20:58.180
I was only trying to frighten you.

01:20:58.240 --> 01:20:59.100
I won't hurt you, Sandra.

01:20:59.450 --> 01:20:59.970
I know, Jane.

01:21:00.160 --> 01:21:00.600
I know.

01:21:02.200 --> 01:21:03.790
Jim, move.

01:21:04.650 --> 01:21:10.480
If you do, I'm not going back there in that pen for the rest of my life.

01:21:11.710 --> 01:21:12.150
Hate me.

01:21:12.880 --> 01:21:13.870
No, Jim, no.

01:21:14.370 --> 01:21:14.890
Yes, you do.

01:21:15.110 --> 01:21:15.790
So does Sandra.

01:21:16.720 --> 01:21:17.700
I heard enough just now.

01:21:18.780 --> 01:21:21.020
I don't like people to hate me.

01:21:21.470 --> 01:21:22.430
Nobody hates you, Jim.

01:21:22.650 --> 01:21:24.670
Let's talk about this, quietly.

01:21:25.100 --> 01:21:27.020
This could only make a lot of trouble for all of us.

01:21:27.860 --> 01:21:29.060
No, no!

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:30.800
I'm going my own way.

01:21:30.980 --> 01:21:33.540
I warn you, don't try to stop me.

01:22:42.250 --> 01:22:43.150
It was all my fault.

01:22:44.410 --> 01:22:45.270
You shouldn't blame yourself.

01:22:47.040 --> 01:22:50.030
I was so stubborn, so suspicious.

01:22:51.500 --> 01:22:52.260
Hard to convince.

01:22:56.300 --> 01:22:58.950
No, I didn't trust you either.

01:23:01.060 --> 01:23:01.120
Thank you.
